INSERT OR IGNORE INTO threads(category_id,user_id,title,slug,body,pinned) SELECT c.id,u.id,'Advanced studies: the Living Force and the Cosmic Force','jedi-force-advanced','The Living Force concerns the interconnected life of beings in the present. The Cosmic Force concerns the larger continuity and destiny of existence. These concepts are explored through Qui-Gon Jinn and Yoda, especially in The Clone Wars season six.

Qui-Gon''s approach emphasizes attention to the present rather than rigid adherence to predictions. Yoda''s later journey challenges the assumption that mastery consists simply of accumulating techniques. The preservation of identity after death is a fictional spiritual achievement, not a real-world claim.

Study questions: How can awareness of the present coexist with responsibility for the future? What distinguishes intuition from wishful thinking? Compare The Phantom Menace and The Clone Wars episodes Voices, Destiny and Sacrifice.',0 FROM categories c CROSS JOIN users u WHERE c.slug='jedi-temple' AND u.username='knightfall' AND u.role='god';
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO threads(category_id,user_id,title,slug,body,pinned) SELECT c.id,u.id,'Jedi training: initiates, Padawans, Knights and Masters','jedi-training-ranks','The prequel-era Jedi Order trains young initiates in communal settings before individual apprenticeships. A Padawan studies under a mentor, developing judgment alongside technical skills. Knighthood represents independent responsibility; mastery concerns teaching, wisdom and service rather than merely combat ability. Council membership is a distinct institutional position.

The path varies across historical eras and continuities. Anakin''s unusual admission and disputed advancement illustrate tensions between exceptional ability and institutional expectations.

Study assignment: design a fictional mentorship curriculum with ethical reasoning, conflict resolution, research, reflection and accountability. Explain how readiness could be assessed without rewarding blind obedience.',0 FROM categories c CROSS JOIN users u WHERE c.slug='jedi-temple' AND u.username='knightfall' AND u.role='god';
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO threads(category_id,user_id,title,slug,body,pinned) SELECT c.id,u.id,'Jedi artifacts: holocrons, kyber and lightsaber traditions','jedi-artifacts-traditions','Holocrons preserve teachings and knowledge in fictional Force-sensitive devices. Kyber crystals are central to lightsaber construction in modern canon and are associated with a relationship between the crystal and its wielder. The lightsaber symbolizes responsibility as well as martial capability.

The Gathering arc of The Clone Wars depicts young Jedi seeking crystals and learning patience, cooperation and self-knowledge. The seven named lightsaber forms are developed across franchise reference material and Legends; avoid assuming every detail applies equally to current canon.

Discussion: what makes an artifact sacred: its material, its history, its use or the commitments of its keeper? This is a lore study, not a real weapon construction guide.',0 FROM categories c CROSS JOIN users u WHERE c.slug='jedi-temple' AND u.username='knightfall' AND u.role='god';
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO threads(category_id,user_id,title,slug,body,pinned) SELECT c.id,u.id,'Jedi case studies: Qui-Gon, Obi-Wan, Ahsoka and Luke','jedi-masters-case-studies','Qui-Gon illustrates independent judgment within an institution. Obi-Wan illustrates loyalty, duty and the difficulty of reconciling personal bonds with responsibility. Ahsoka''s departure from the Order demonstrates that conscience and institutional membership can diverge. Luke''s decision to seek redemption rather than surrender to hatred challenges the assumption that victory requires destroying an opponent.

Primary viewing: The Phantom Menace; Revenge of the Sith; The Clone Wars season five finale; Return of the Jedi.

Assignment: compare each character''s response to authority, uncertainty and attachment. Identify one strength and one limitation in each approach. Avoid treating any character as morally infallible.',0 FROM categories c CROSS JOIN users u WHERE c.slug='jedi-temple' AND u.username='knightfall' AND u.role='god';
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO threads(category_id,user_id,title,slug,body,pinned) SELECT c.id,u.id,'Advanced studies: the dark side and the illusion of mastery','sith-force-advanced','The dark side is depicted as a path that draws on fear, anger, aggression and desire. Its attraction lies partly in the promise of immediate control when uncertainty feels intolerable. The narrative repeatedly contrasts apparent mastery of external circumstances with increasing dependence on destructive emotions.

Anakin''s pursuit of forbidden knowledge in Revenge of the Sith illustrates the danger of treating extraordinary promises as evidence. Sidious exploits his fear rather than resolving it.

Study questions: Can a person distinguish an empowering emotion from an emotion that controls them? Why is the promise of certainty attractive? Compare the dark-side cave in The Empire Strikes Back with Anakin''s decisions in Revenge of the Sith.',0 FROM categories c CROSS JOIN users u WHERE c.slug='order-of-the-sith' AND u.username='knightfall' AND u.role='god';
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO threads(category_id,user_id,title,slug,body,pinned) SELECT c.id,u.id,'Sith historical survey: ancient orders, empires and succession','sith-historical-survey','The Sith have multiple historical incarnations across Star Wars storytelling. Legends develops extensive histories of ancient Sith civilizations, rival empires and conflicts with the Jedi. The modern canon confirms ancient Sith history but does not automatically adopt every Legends chronology or biography.

Suggested Legends reading: Tales of the Jedi, Knights of the Old Republic and the Darth Bane trilogy. Canon viewing: The Clone Wars episode Sacrifice and the sequel trilogy''s treatment of Sith legacy.

Research assignment: construct two separate timelines, marking each entry Canon or Legends and identifying its source. Where accounts differ, record the difference rather than inventing a reconciliation.',0 FROM categories c CROSS JOIN users u WHERE c.slug='order-of-the-sith' AND u.username='knightfall' AND u.role='god';
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO threads(category_id,user_id,title,slug,body,pinned) SELECT c.id,u.id,'Sith artifacts: holocrons, temples and corrupted kyber','sith-artifacts-traditions','Sith holocrons and temples function as repositories of dangerous or restricted knowledge within fictional lore. Their secrecy reflects the order''s concern with preserving power and controlling succession. In current canon, red lightsaber crystals are associated with the fictional process of bleeding kyber; older Legends accounts include different explanations, including synthetic crystals.

Reference works: Star Wars Rebels, Twilight of the Apprentice; Darth Vader (2017) comics. Study how artifacts express a character''s values and relationship to power.

Discussion: does restricting knowledge preserve it, or make its custodians unaccountable? This lesson concerns fictional symbolism, not real occult or weapon techniques.',0 FROM categories c CROSS JOIN users u WHERE c.slug='order-of-the-sith' AND u.username='knightfall' AND u.role='god';
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO threads(category_id,user_id,title,slug,body,pinned) SELECT c.id,u.id,'Sith case studies: Bane, Maul, Dooku and Sidious','sith-masters-case-studies','Bane represents institutional redesign through concentrated succession. Maul illustrates how obsession with revenge can consume an identity long after its original purpose is gone. Dooku demonstrates how disillusionment with a flawed institution can become complicity in a worse one. Sidious represents the pursuit of domination as an end in itself.

Study sources: the Darth Bane trilogy (Legends), The Clone Wars, Tales of the Jedi and Revenge of the Sith (Canon).

Assignment: distinguish each character''s stated goals from the consequences of their choices. Compare independence, loyalty, resentment and ambition. Consider whether their methods undermine their own objectives.',0 FROM categories c CROSS JOIN users u WHERE c.slug='order-of-the-sith' AND u.username='knightfall' AND u.role='god';